						(xy 0 0) (xy 0 1.27) (xy -1.016 1.905) (xy 0 2.54) (xy 1.016 1.905) (xy 0 1.27)
					)
					(stroke
						(width 0)
						(type default)
					)
					(fill
						(type none)
					)
				)
			)
			(embedded_fonts no)
		)
	)
	(text "Pre-regulator: U16 holds PRE_FB at 0.5 V and runs in forced PWM\n(PS/SYNC high). U19 makes PRE_FB = 0.200 x V_PRE + 0.146 x VREF\n- 0.191 x LDO_OUT, so V_PRE = 0.672 V + 0.956 x LDO_OUT (calculated):\n0.64 V above the output at 0.8 V and 0.45 V at 5.0 V, also while a\ndevice holds the output above the set-point. A short at the output\nfolds V_PRE back to 0.84 V (simulated).\nR65, R64 and C55: 0.62 ms low-pass that keeps the sense out of\nthe loop of U16. D13 lets V_PRE follow a fast rise of the output\nat once. C52: phase lead for U19. R62 empties C42, C45 and\nC50 within about 0.2 s while U16 is off (calculated)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.38 16.002 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "04a7555a-0b82-54bd-8f99-1c2cd750968f")
	)
	(text "U16 land pattern: lead pads agree with TI drawing 4210895-2/E;\ncenter pad 1.7 x 3.3 mm against 1.58 x 2.85 mm accepted; via\narray in the pad at layout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 92.964 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3abf4f31-c0cb-519f-8dd0-c57f79358a05")
	)
	(text "Linear regulator: U18 takes IN from V_PRE through FB1, VCONTROL\nfrom +13V5 through R61 and D10, and SET from U17. Both supply\npins are rated 0.3 V below OUT (datasheet): D11 carries the current\nwhile OUT is above IN, and D10 lets C47 hold VCONTROL up at\npower-off. D12 keeps LDO_OUT above about -0.2 V (estimate).\nR69 is the minimum load: 3.7 mA at 0.8 V, 6.9 mA at 5.0 V\n(calculated); it also takes the leakage of D11.\nC43 and R59 damp the resonance of FB1 with C46.\nDesign current: 1.0 A up to 2.0 V, falling to 0.6 A at 5.0 V\n(calculated, not yet confirmed on a board).\nTP25, TP20: probe grounds at the linear regulator and at the pre-regulator."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 16.002 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d45e650-8025-54ba-ae8a-158fe4554a45")
	)
	(text "On the board: R67 and R62 connect at\npin 1 of FB1, R65 and D13 at the\nOUT pins of U18; R55 sits next to\nR56 and R57 next to R58."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.81 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "89fa7011-5e9c-5aef-9e04-2e14c6de2dce")
	)
	(text "Set-point: U15 runs at gain 2 from VREF / 2 (R55,\nR56), reference input buffered: frame 0x5000 | code.\nU17 has a gain of 2.1: LDO_OUT = 10 mV + code x\n1.2817 mV before calibration, and no frame gives more\nthan 5.26 V (5.39 V at the tolerance limits,\ncalculated). R54 and C41: 10 ms, so the set-point\nmoves at 0.52 V/ms at most."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 168.402 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c290ce2e-5a96-5b02-b932-101e0d7e30d1")
	)
	(text "Enable: SMU_ON reaches U16 through Q1 only while\n5V_OK is high. When +5V falls below 3.83 V to 4.00 V\nthe supervisor opens Q1 and R53 pulls the pin low:\nthe pre-regulator is shed without the firmware.\nWith +5V at 4.25 V the pin gets 2.36 V (calculated,\ngate threshold estimated; it needs 1.2 V, datasheet).\nStart: DAC at the 0.80 V code for 200 ms with SMU_ON\nlow, then SMU_ON high; the output switch closes last."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 16.002 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f7ac02d2-9afd-5d7b-bf05-016cee816ca0")
	)
